{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each element stands in a tower of levels, one more with probability 1\/4, so a search skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ahead on the upper levels and finishes on the bottom one. Lookup, insertion and removal take"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time, with no rebalancing. Every link also records how many elements it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes, so the elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like an array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"list[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"code":["var numbers: SkipList = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","numbers.insert(4)","Array(numbers)                \/\/ [1, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9]","numbers.lowerBound(5)         \/\/ 3, the index of 5","numbers[1]                    \/\/ 3"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tower heights come from a random number generator given at creation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator"},{"type":"text","text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The list draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heights as its original."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The elements and their towers live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the list holds fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SkipLists\/SK","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/Sl","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/Se","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/SE","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/SQ","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/SH","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/Sk","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/ST","doc:\/\/SkipLists\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:9SkipLists0A4ListV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SkipLists\/SkipList.swift#L29","fileName":"SkipList.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct","title":"